#N Brian's Brain glider
#C Four cells that travel one cell per generation, for ever: the firing pair
#C leads and the refractory pair trails. Brian's Brain has no still lifes at
#C all, so everything in it is either moving or dying.
#C Constructed for this library, found by searching random soups. Twenty
#C thousand of them turned up no oscillator, which is why this is a glider.
x = 2, y = 2, rule = B2/S/C3
2B$2A!
